# The image build needs the Rust workspace plus the benchmarks corpus the
# library embeds at compile time (quality.rs include_dir!s ../benchmarks/
# corpus). Everything heavy or desktop-bound stays out of the build
# context. src-tauri/benches must also ride along: the manifest declares
# the bench target explicitly, so cargo needs the file even to parse the
# workspace.
.git
.github
node_modules
dist
output
docs
design
tests
examples
action
docker
src-tauri/target
src-tauri/gen
src-tauri/fuzz
src-tauri/tests
src-tauri/examples
